The report said a new HomePod mini, new Apple TV 4K, and an all-new Apple smart home hub <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/30/apple-home-products-coming-on-october-13/">will all be announced on Tuesday, October 13</a>, but it sounds like a new version of the full-sized HomePod will not be unveiled until a later date. If and when it does finally arrive, expect support for the more intelligent Siri AI to be a key new feature.<br/>
<br/>
Siri AI support would require a faster chip—the current HomePod uses the Apple Watch Series 7's S7 chip. Other likely upgrades include improved audio quality, new color options, and Apple's custom-designed N1 chip with Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6 support.<br/>
<br/>
The full-sized HomePod is a relatively niche product, but it is a convenient choice for Apple fans with home theater setups. A pair of HomePods can be set as an Apple TV 4K's default audio output, allowing for stereo sound.<br/>
<br/>
